[Meht]a blocked the merger on June 23 when he granted a Federal Trade Commission request to delay the transaction. The[ FTC] had sued the companies in February, saying the deal would give Sysco an[ oversized] share of an industry[ where] it’s already the biggest player.
In arguments before Me[ht]a in May, the two sides clashed over the scope of the market in which the companies compete. Sysco and US[ Foods] argued that the commission was relying on a �[�]tortured�[�] analysis, ignoring the variety of distribution channels available to customers.
Sysco said on Monday that it weighed embarking on an appeal but decided against it.
